The attached image, Figure 7D, is a Western blot illustrating the secretion and processing of IL-1β by dendritic cells. It shows that in conditions where Nano-11 is combined with LPS, the 30 kD pro-IL-1β (visible in cell lysate) is cleaved into its active 17 kD form, which is then secreted into the supernatant. This confirms Nano-11's ability to induce biologically active IL-1β, a key pro-inflammatory cytokine, thereby contributing to its role as an effective vaccine adjuvant.